  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nOn Saturday, lingering moisture and instability will be present\nover the region, with rain chances favored mainly north of U.S.\nHighway 90. Rain chances should end Saturday evening with some\nbrief clearing of skies expected. Confidence in dry weather for\nSunday and Monday remains high as mid-level ridging builds over\nthe area in advance of a deepening upper trough over the western\nU.S. \n\nThe medium range operational models are showing some better\nagreement with respect to the mid-level flow pattern over the\nsouthern U.S. plains early next week. A positive tilt trough axis\napproaches from the west Monday and eventually becomes neutral to\nslightly negative while traversing through Texas into the lower MS\nriver valley through Wednesday. We've seen some timing differences\nwith the frontal passage with the latest models now showing the\ncold front moving through during the daytime hours. This would\nlikely yield a line of showers and storms with the front and will\ncontinue to monitor for the possibility of some strong storms\ngiven adequate shear and some instability.\n\nGusty northwest winds behind the front Tuesday night into \nWednesday will bring some cooler and drier air to the region with \nhighs easing back into the upper 60s and mid 70s along with lows \nin the upper 40s and 50s for Wednesday and Thursday.",
